From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 22:52:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08176/11362] [outer-loop] ARC generalization corrigenda:
 adapter-free search cost was a constant, not a measurement

Adversarial review of exp6092/exp6093; every correction re-verified independently before
being applied. Additive only -- no prior number removed.

exp6094 (new): the dev-twin cell wrote `search_cost = args.max_expansions` in BOTH treatment
branches and never passed `stats=` to graph_explore_solve_v2, so all 25 adapter-free rows
carried the BUDGET and 15 carried the label `max_expansions_exhausted` -- an assertion the
code could not make. Re-measured with stats={}: 13 of 15 genuinely exhausted; sc25 stopped
at 24 expansions / 1 distinct state and g50t at 4100 / 843, identically at 6000 and at 30000.
For those two the 5x probe was vacuous and the failure is a frontier collapse, not a search
wall. On the 10 games both arms solve, the generic explorer needs a median 155x more
expansions for the same move count.

exp6093 corrections: the dev-twin sign test is post-hoc (the pre-registration covers only the
scored arms); the 24/25->10/25 drop bundles a search-engine swap and a verifier warm start
(12 of 25 controls loaded one, not 15) alongside per-game knowledge; move-count parity is not
proven optimality; HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS is an unenumerated id-keyed channel (dead under
LLM-off); headline units renamed so 4-in-400-actions is not read against 183-unbounded.

exp6092 corrections: `cautions` are NOT identical public vs hidden -- n=8 both ways but 8/8
content-disjoint on sb26/tn36/r11l/lf52 (5/8 on wa30), because _cautions_from puts ranked
dead-ends before general_gotchas under an 8-cap. They are excluded because nothing reads them,
not because they match. Adds the transition corpus as a not-counted diluted cross-game prior
(22758 rows, 24 aggregate keys, max leave-one-game-out shift 0.069). Corrects the arc_e3 dir
count (27, not 25) and the dev-twin closure size (160, not 129).

No behaviour changed, no game played, nothing submitted, no source read, CPU only.

